reviews.body:
Adversarial contract review completed against the committed diff and green Governance CI.

Verified:
- controller/kernel state remains runtime-neutral; tmux/PTY/WebSocket/process handles are adapter-local;
- observe and interactive authority are mutually enforced, with `send_input` required only for interactive mode;
- reconnect requires current workspace fence and unchanged session generation;
- minimal bootstrap is bounded to 4096 bytes and typed argv/env references, with shell-metacharacter rejection fixtures;
- raw terminal output is non-canonical and forbidden from persistence; lifecycle and input digests remain auditable;
- detach cannot cancel an attempt without a separate controller command;
- tmux default and optional browser PTY share parity assertions.

Local dependency-free, optimized-mode, Python/JSON, whitespace, and credential-pattern checks passed. Governance CI passed. No change requested at this stacked-contract stage. Protected-main independent approval and parent-stack ordering remain required before merge.
